/ Main entry point for the PLang builder
/ Transforms .goal files (natural language) into .pr files (JSON the Runtime executes)
/ Parameters: %path% - folder to build (default: ".")
Build

- set default %path% = "/"
/ The goals saved with steps the build could not fix are collected in %brokenGoals% (BuildGoal's LeaveBroken adds
/ each) and named at the end. Started here, in an existing step: a step is matched to its earlier build by its
/ position, so a step inserted among the others would make every one after it build again.
- variable.set(Name=%traceGoals%, Value=[]); variable.set(Name=%brokenGoals%, Value=[])
- set channel "builder" call BuilderChannel
- call EmitBuildEvent kind="build-path", path=%path%
- build.load, write to %app%
- build.goals path=%path%, write to %goals%
- call EmitBuildEvent kind="goals-found", goals=%goals%
- loop.foreach(Collection=%goals%); goal.call(Name="/system/builder/BuildGoal", Parameter=[{goal: %item%}])
- build.unreached
- save %traceGoals% to file '/.build/traces/%!trace.id%/manifest.json'
- build.appSave
/ A goal was saved with broken steps: the build ends failed, holding each such goal's refusal whole as a cause, so the
/ error page names every goal, its step and why.
- condition.if(Left=%brokenGoals.count%, Operator=">", Right=0) { error.throw(Message="the build left goals with steps it could not fix", Key="StepsBroken", Status=400, Cause=%brokenGoals%, FixSuggestion="fix the words and build again") }
